      "id": "be-s12m-synthesizing-example-c2",
      "heading": "Monopoly or monopolistic competition",
      "explanation_md": "Facing **P = 100 - Q**:\n\n- **MR = 100 - 2Q**; set 100 - 2Q = 8Q, so **Q = 10**\n- **P = 100 - 10 = $90**\n- Profit = (90)(10) - (125 + 4(100)) = **$375**\n\n**Implications:** a **monopolist** will not face entry unless patents or other barriers are removed. A **monopolistically competitive** firm should expect others to **clone** its product, so **profits decline over time**.",
