    {
      "id": "be-s12m-synthesizing-example-q-5bf1855f",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "A firm has C(Q) = 125 + 4Q². Find the profit-maximizing output, price and profit if (a) it is a price taker and other firms charge $40, and (b) it is a monopolist facing P = 100 - Q. Discuss the implications.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**MC = 8Q** in both cases.\n\n**(a) Price taker:** MR = P = 40 = 8Q, so **Q = 5**. Cost = 125 + 100 = $225, revenue = $200, profit = **-$25**. Expect **exit** in the long run.\n\n**(b) Monopoly:** MR = 100 - 2Q = 8Q, so **Q = 10**, **P = $90**. Profit = 900 - (125 + 400) = **$375**. A monopolist faces no entry unless its barriers are removed; a monopolistically competitive firm with the same demand would see rivals clone it and profits decline.",
      "rubric": [
        {
          "point": "MC = 8Q",
          "source_ref": "be--session-12#44"
        },
        {
          "point": "Price taker Q = 5 and loss $25",
          "source_ref": "be--session-12#45"
        },
        {
          "point": "Monopoly Q = 10, P = $90",
          "source_ref": "be--session-12#46"
        },
        {
          "point": "Profit $375 and implications",
          "source_ref": "be--session-12#46"
        }
      ],
